workedExamples.solution_text:
Divide $6$ by each nonzero input.

| $x$ | $-6$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $3$ | $6$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $f(x)$ | $-1$ | $-2$ | $-6$ | Undefined | $6$ | $2$ | $1$ |

Plot the points and draw two smooth branches approaching the coordinate axes.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[black,<->] (-7,0)--(7,0);
\draw[black,<->] (0,-7)--(0,7);
\path (7,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,7) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-6,-3,3,6}{\draw[black] (\v,-0.12)--(\v,0.12);\path (\v,-0.12) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};\draw[black] (-0.12,\v)--(0.12,\v);\path (-0.12,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=0.9:6.7,samples=100] plot (\x,{6/(\x)});
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-6.7:-0.9,samples=100] plot (\x,{6/(\x)});
\foreach \x/\y in {-6/-1,-3/-2,-1/-6,1/6,3/2,6/1}{\fill[curveblue] (\x,\y) circle (1.2pt);}
\path (4,4) node {$y=\dfrac{6}{x}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Positive inputs give positive outputs and negative inputs give negative outputs, so the branches lie in Quadrants $1$ and $3$.

As positive $x$ increases, $\dfrac{6}{x}$ stays positive and becomes smaller: as $x\to\infty$, $f(x)\to0^+$, from above.

As negative $x$ increases in magnitude, $\dfrac{6}{x}$ stays negative and becomes closer to zero: as $x\to-\infty$, $f(x)\to0^-$, from below.

At $x=0$, the expression is $\dfrac{6}{0}$, which is undefined because division by zero is not possible.

The reciprocal constants are $\dfrac{5}{2}>0$ for $f$ and $-\dfrac{5}{2}<0$ for $g$.

| Function | Quadrants | As $x\to\infty$ | As $x\to-\infty$ |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| $f(x)=\dfrac{5}{2x}$ | $1$ and $3$ | $f(x)\to0^+$, from above | $f(x)\to0^-$, from below |
| $g(x)=-\dfrac{5}{2x}$ | $2$ and $4$ | $g(x)\to0^-$, from below | $g(x)\to0^+$, from above |

At each nonzero input, the two outputs have equal magnitudes and opposite signs. Both curves approach the axes $x=0$ and $y=0$.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=7mm,y=7mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{curveblue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{curvered}{HTML}{EF6068}
\draw[black,<->] (-4.5,0)--(4.5,0);
\draw[black,<->] (0,-4.5)--(0,4.5);
\path (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$} (0,4.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \v in {-4,-2,2,4}{\draw[black] (\v,-0.08)--(\v,0.08);\path (\v,-0.08) node[below,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};\draw[black] (-0.08,\v)--(0.08,\v);\path (-0.08,\v) node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] {$\v$};}
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=0.6:4.2,samples=100] plot (\x,{2.5/(\x)});
\draw[curveblue,thick,<->,domain=-4.2:-0.6,samples=100] plot (\x,{2.5/(\x)});
\draw[curvered,thick,dashed,<->,domain=0.6:4.2,samples=100] plot (\x,{-2.5/(\x)});
\draw[curvered,thick,dashed,<->,domain=-4.2:-0.6,samples=100] plot (\x,{-2.5/(\x)});
\path (2.6,2.8) node[text=curveblue] {$f(x)=\dfrac{5}{2x}$};
\path (-2.6,2.8) node[text=curvered] {$g(x)=-\dfrac{5}{2x}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

